# Build context for BOTH images.
#
# Docker reads the .dockerignore next to the build CONTEXT, and infra/compute/index.ts sets
# `context: repoRoot` for web-ui-image and workers-image alike — so this file is the one that
# applies, and apps/web-ui/.dockerignore is never consulted by either build.
#
# Two things this buys:
#
#  1. The docker-build provider hashes the context to decide whether an image is stale. With the
#     whole repo in scope, editing infra/compute/index.ts invalidated that hash and rebuilt AND
#     redeployed both ECS services for a change that cannot affect either image.
#  2. The context was 2.8 GB, almost all of it node_modules (2.3 GB) and apps/web-ui/.next
#     (232 MB) — uploaded to the daemon on every build to be discarded.
#
# Safe because between them the two Dockerfiles copy only four paths from the host:
#   apps/web-ui/   apps/workers/   libs/prisma/   tsconfig.base.json
# Everything else in here is outside those, or is a build output regenerated inside the image.
#
# Before adding a pattern that could touch one of those four, check it: build a throwaway image
# against this same context that COPYs the four paths and asserts the files each Dockerfile needs
# still arrive (package.json + bun.lock, apps/web-ui/app, next.config.mjs, docker-entrypoint.sh,
# public/, apps/workers/src, libs/prisma/schema.prisma + migrations, tsconfig.base.json). That is
# how this file was validated — the context went from 2.8 GB to 12 MB with all of them intact.

# ── Dependencies: every image runs its own `bun install` ─────────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# ── Build outputs, regenerated inside the image ─────────────────────────────
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
**/.turbo
.nx

# ── Not copied by any Dockerfile ────────────────────────────────────────────
# infra/ is the reason this file exists: Pulumi source cannot affect an app image.
infra
docs
# The Playwright project. Its specs change often and no image contains them.
apps/web-ui-e2e
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# ── Local env files. Nothing COPYs them (they sit at the repo root, outside the
#    four copied paths), so this only keeps the build cache stable when secrets change.
.env
.env.*

# ── Test and tooling artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT `**/coverage`: that matches a directory of that name at any depth, which also
# excluded app/api/scaling-audit/coverage/route.ts — a real API route. It was then
# missing from every built image and 404'd wherever it was deployed. Coverage output
# only lands at a project root, so match it there.
/coverage
apps/*/coverage
libs/*/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.lcov

# ── Noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*.pem
